  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 124 AM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nMain concern through the weekend continues to be the heat. Heat \nindices up to 114 are forecast across many locations this afternoon. \nThus, a Heat Advisory has been issued from Noon to 6 pm for most of \nS TX. A few places may briefly exceed 115, but most places will \nremain below 115. Major to extreme risk of heat related impacts will \ncontinue into early next week and Heat Advisories may be needed at \ntimes.\n\nLess moisture and mid level ridging across northeastern Mexico and \nwest TX will lead to very low rain chances today. Rain chances \nincrease slightly Sunday in response to the ridge being nudged \nnorthward as an inverted trough shifts west across S TX. This will \nallow for a slightly more active sea breeze. Isolated sea breeze \nconvection is expected early next week with the potential for \nincreased activity by mid to late week. Models have been varying on \nwhich day has the best chance of rain, but it does look like \nsometime between Wednesday and Friday may see medium to high rain \nchances in response to a surge of deep moisture from the gulf waters \ncombined with a mid level short wave.",
